  "name": "Example: Representing Negative Angles in the Coordinate Plane",
  "problem": "Construct the angle $-225^\\circ$ in the coordinate plane in the usual way.",
  "worked_solution": "First, we recall that:\n\n- An angle in the standard position has its initial side on the positive $x$-axis, and its vertex lies at the origin.\n\n- It rotates such that a positive angle is measured counter-clockwise, and a negative angle is measured clockwise.\n\nTherefore, the correct diagram is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14222483/assets/3304f581480780d7139bac50ded646f78a8c8c344c0184ad81955bcc83acbe72.png)",
